= Congressional outlook

House — Democrats: [+ dem_house_seats +] seats; Republicans: [+ gop_house_seats +] seats
Senate — Democrats: [+ dem_senate_seats +] seats; Republicans: [+ gop_senate_seats +] seats

[? if dem_house : **Democrats control the House.** ?][? if not dem_house : **Republicans control the House.** ?]
[? if dem_senate : **Democrats control the Senate.** ?][? if not dem_senate : **Republicans control the Senate.** ?]
]

= Democratic primary (if applicable)

DSA-aligned Left: [+ primary_delegate_share_insurgent +]%
Progressive: [+ primary_delegate_share_progressive +]%
Labor Left: [+ primary_delegate_share_labor_left +]%
Establishment: [+ primary_delegate_share_establishment_dem +]%
Blue Dog: [+ primary_delegate_share_blue_dog +]%

**Nomination lead:** [+ primary_winner_faction +]


= Notes

- These projections are computed from the same demographic-by-class normalizer used
  across the game (see election_algorithm.scene.dry). If you want to trigger a
  full election computation (primary/general/midterm), use the dedicated
  election flows that call election_algorithm's sub-algorithms so turnout,
  bloc math, and seat-swing rules are applied.

- After reviewing results, go back to the main game.

- @back: Return

